# LICENSE

The `.xsd` files under `v2_1/` and `v3_0/` are verbatim, unmodified copies of the
official BCF-XML schemas published by buildingSMART International:

  https://github.com/buildingSMART/BCF-XML
    v2_1/  <- branch `release_2_1`, `Schemas/`
    v3_0/  <- branch `release_3_0`, `Schemas/`

Only the schemas the tests actually validate against are kept: `markup.xsd`,
`visinfo.xsd`, `project.xsd`, `version.xsd`, plus `shared-types.xsd`, which
BCF 3.0's schemas pull in with `<xs:include>`. Upstream also publishes
`extensions.xsd` (both versions) and `documents.xsd` (3.0); neither is
vendored, because nothing here validates against them and an unused copy only
goes stale.

